	<section_number>15.2-1700</section_number>
	<catch_line>Preservation of peace and good order</catch_line>
	<text>
		Any locality may provide for the protection of its inhabitants and property and for the preservation of peace and good order therein.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 15-556; 1962, c. 623, § 15.1-137; 1997, c. 587.</history>
